silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_06_circuit_imprint_transport_sections_01_circuit_3_semantic_dexterity_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'Circuit3SemanticDexterityConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the household's named typed-arrow set. The bare math anchor-node name is resolved to a concrete household-or-clinic node of the Mittens vet-clinic transport scenario so a zero-math reader can ground the reading; the transport functor F preserves the typed arrows that bind this node into the larger commutative diagram.; also, the clinic's named typed-arrow set. The bare math anchor-node name is resolved to a concrete household-or-clinic node of the Mittens vet-clinic transport scenario so a zero-math reader can ground the reading; the transport functor F preserves the typed arrows that bind this node into the larger commutative diagram.." .
